# Keep the JUnit fixtures byte-for-byte as the runners produced them.
#
# GitHub's windows-latest image sets core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite every
# fixture's line endings on checkout. The steering rule is that each parser dialect needs
# a *real* fixture file, because hand-written XML that happens to parse proves nothing
# about Maven's actual output -- and a file git has reformatted is no longer that runner's
# actual output either. `-text` disables all newline translation for these paths.
*.xml -text
tests/fixtures/** -text

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they will not execute under sh on a Windows runner.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The compiled dashboard bundle is committed and CI fails on any diff against a
# rebuild, so it must not be rewritten on checkout either.
src/flaky_detective/web/static/** -text

# Databases and archives are binary. Named explicitly rather than relying on
# auto-detection, since a corrupted SQLite file fails in confusing ways.
*.db binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
